1916	{"artifactId":"ISSUE-5f7a7cb95b643ae5","entry":{"id":"50d1c05d","text":"ADDITIONAL EVIDENCE for the decision this issue already frames (base at approval time vs at build time), from a second trigger: TIME DRIFT rather than sibling sweep. Filed here rather than as a new issue because the mechanism and the decision are identical — a base fixed at approval does not describe the Story when the build happens later.\n\nObserved on 93081bff S001 (2026-10-04), back-filled two days after its plan was approved. The change set came back with 169 entries, naming OTHER Stories' BUILD records, because rangeBase..HEAD swept every commit since approval. A second attempt produced 2 unrelated entries. Neither describes the Story, whose real change set is 17 files across 12 commits, derived by hand from its own commits for the ledger record.\n\nTwo things this adds to the decision. First, the failure is UNBOUNDED in the time-drift case: the later the build, the wider the range, with no upper limit — so \"keep it at approval time\" needs an answer for drift and not only for siblings. Second, by this issue's own sibling framing the two triggers would be fixed by the same choice, so settling one settles both; if the base moves to build time, both the sibling collapse and the drift sweep go away together.\n\nAlso recorded: no test covers a STALE base. range-base.test.ts covers the resolver's precedence, and the build-step suite exercises the prompt-validation case where base and HEAD sit a commit or two apart. The drift case is untested, which is why it reached a real ledger record. Raised as a MED coverage finding in CR-93081bff91ae5108-s1.","actor":{"id":"legacy:claude-opus-5-controller","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"claude-opus-5 (controller)"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:16:38.651Z","feedback":[],"kind":"revision-request","anchor":{"section":".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5f7a7cb95b643ae5.json"}}}
